7. When describing the semantics of any programming language, mention is usually made of Name and Attributes, Bindings and Scope of Bindings. What do these refer to? (5 marks)
8. Below is a C-style pseudocode.

    int x;
    void p(void) {
        char y;
        ...
        { int i;
          ...
        }
    }
    void q(void) {
        double z;
        ...
    }
    main() {
        int w[10];
        ...
    }

a. Copy the pseudocode and use brackets to show the binding scopes of the names you can identify. (4 marks)
b. Rewrite the pseudocode in either Java or Python. (6 marks).
